      "writtenOn": "2022-04-26T18:03:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe I\u0027m misunderstanding, but blindly replacing `as_` with `into()` doesn\u0027t work:\n```\nerror[E0277]: the trait bound `i32: From\u003cusize\u003e` is not satisfied\n   --\u003e external/crosvm/base/src/unix/sock_ctrl_msg.rs:123:34\n    |\n123 |     msg.msg_iovlen \u003d iovec.len().into();\n    |                                  ^^^^ the trait `From\u003cusize\u003e` is not implemented for `i32`\n    |\n```\n\nTruncating is unavoidable here, musl uses posix\u0027s `int` definition of `msg_iovlen`, not glibc\u0027s `size_t`.",
